  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trase: Intelligence for sustainable trade</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of the project is to analyse and publish information on the deforestation risk in a number of commodity value chains which originate in rain forest countries: 

Soy, corn and beef from Brazil, Argentina, Paraguay and soy from Bolivia, palm oil from Indonesia, cocao from Brazil, Ecuador, Ivory Coast, Ghana, Indonesia, coffee from Brazil, Colombia, Indonesia, Vietnam, shrimp from Ecuador, Indonesia, and pulp from Indonesia. In addition, trase looks at domestic value chains for beef in Brazil. 

The aim is to consumers and other market players knowledgable about this global value chains.</narrative>
  </description>
